// One empty bucket. A list literal builds a fresh list on every call, which is
// what makes this a bucket factory rather than one shared list handed out
// repeatedly -- lists are references, so the difference is the whole index.
new_bucket() {
  int[] bkt = [];
} return int[] bkt;

// A prime, so that the final `%` mixes all sixteen bits of the hash rather
// than keeping the low ones. About 1300 names in this compiler, so five or so
// per bucket.
idx_n() {
} return int 251;

str_hash(string s) {
  int hv = 0;
  hv = hash_loop(s, 0, hv);
} return int hv % idx_n();
